{#- formulas/backup-offsite — nightly `restic copy` of every restic repo on
   the NAS share (formulas/backup, <source_base>/<minion>) into one offsite
   repo per minion at <repository>/<minion> (S3-compatible object storage).
   Runs on one host that mounts the whole share — salt-master, which
   resolves every pillar secret anyway, so holding the source passwords
   there adds no exposure.

   repository: restic repo base, e.g. s3:https://<namespace>.compat.
   objectstorage.<region>.oraclecloud.com/<bucket> (IaC-opentofu oci output
   restic_offsite_repository). region: AWS_DEFAULT_REGION for the S3 API.
   s3_bucket_lookup: OCI's compat API wants path-style requests.

   `password` is the offsite repos' own one (OpenBao restic/offsite) —
   independent of the source passwords, and kept outside the homelab too
   (README "Bootstrap"): with the NAS and OpenBao gone it's the only key.
   access_key_id / secret_access_key: S3 credentials (OCI Customer Secret
   Key of a user that may only touch this bucket).

   `source_password` opens the NAS repos (OpenBao restic/repo);
   `source_passwords` holds per-minion overrides (repos with their own password,
   pillar/backup.sls password_path). Every directory under source_base
   that holds a restic repo is copied — a new minion goes offsite without a
   change here. A repo that fails doesn't stop the others.

   New offsite repos are initialised with the source's chunker parameters
   (--copy-chunker-params), so copies deduplicate like the source.

   keep: forget --keep-<unit> <n> on the offsite repo after each copy, then
   --prune. Longer than the NAS (12 monthly): the copy is the long memory.

   on_calendar: after every nightly backup (02:00 + ≤10 min, ≤45 min) and
   before the Sunday restore test (04:00). retry_lock covers an overlap.

   textfile_dir: node-exporter's textfile collector (backup_offsite_*;
   alerts in pillar/prometheus.sls). ping_slug: Healthchecks check
   <slug>-<minion id> while formulas/healthchecks-ping has a key. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'repository': '',
    'region': '',
    's3_bucket_lookup': 'path',
    'password': '',
    'access_key_id': '',
    'secret_access_key': '',
    'source_base': '/mnt/backups',
    'mount_name': 'backups',
    'source_password': '',
    'source_passwords': {},
    'keep': {'daily': 7, 'weekly': 4, 'monthly': 12},
    'retry_lock': '30m',
    'config_dir': '/etc/restic-offsite',
    'cache_dir': '/var/cache/restic-offsite',
    'restic_bin': '/usr/bin/restic',
    'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    'script': '/usr/local/sbin/restic-offsite',
    'unit': 'restic-offsite',
    'on_calendar': '*-*-* 03:15:00 Europe/Berlin',
    'randomized_delay': '10min',
    'timeout': '3h',
    'textfile_dir': '/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter',
    'metrics_file': 'backup_offsite.prom',
    'ping_slug': 'backup-offsite',
} %}
{%- set offsite = salt['pillar.get']('backup_offsite:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
